 ## Background
-The field of NeRF editing emerged as NeRFs gained popularity for novel view synthesis, with early works focusing on object removal and scene manipulation [G]. Key developments include the introduction of diffusion-guided editing (e.g., RePaint-NeRF, Instruct-NeRF2NeRF) which leveraged 2D generative models to guide 3D optimization [14365-repaint-nerf.md][15089-instruct-nerf2nerf-optimization.md]. Subsequent methods like Blended-NeRF and NeRF-Art introduced techniques for localized editing and stylization using text prompts and volumetric blending [12273-blended-nerf.md][13438-nerf-art.md]. Recent advancements focus on improving multi-view consistency through semantic priors and progressive inpainting strategies [8658-progressive-inpainting-and-erasing.md][14393-semantic-and-language-guided-editing.md].
